    definition: "The percentage change in total revenue between two comparable periods. This metric measures whether the business is expanding its commercial footprint, maintaining position, or contracting. Growth rate is the first-order signal of market demand and competitive relevance. The application reads growth against the sector benchmark for the selected industry profile, because 8% growth is strong in a mature services sector and represents underperformance in a high-growth SaaS market. Declining revenue, in any sector, is the clearest single indicator of deteriorating competitive position.",
