    reading: "The debt-to-equity ratio reveals how the business is capitalized. Higher leverage amplifies both returns and risk. Read alongside cash runway and operating cash flow to assess whether the current debt load is serviceable.",
    areas: "This metric sits in the capital-structure layer of the value chain. When leverage is elevated, examine the debt-service burden — whether interest payments are consuming a material share of operating cash flow; the maturity profile — whether near-term maturities create refinancing risk; and the covenant exposure — whether the business is approaching covenant thresholds that could trigger acceleration or restrict operational flexibility.",
    benchmarks: {"header": ["Profile", "Typical Range", "Elevated", "High Risk"], "rows": [["SaaS / Technology", "0.1–0.5", "0.5–1.0", ">1.5"], ["Services", "0.3–0.8", "0.8–1.5", ">2.0"], ["Manufacturing", "0.5–1.2", "1.2–2.0", ">2.5"], ["Retail", "0.5–1.5", "1.5–2.5", ">3.0"]]},
