    areas: "This metric sits in the stock-management layer of the value chain. When turnover is low, examine: demand forecasting accuracy — whether purchasing or production is misaligned with actual sales velocity; SKU proliferation — whether the catalogue has expanded into items that sell too infrequently to justify the inventory investment; obsolescence exposure — whether a portion of inventory has passed its effective selling window; and the working-capital interaction — slow-moving inventory directly reduces working capital and can compress cash runway.",
    benchmarks: {"header": ["Profile", "Healthy Range", "Concern"], "rows": [["General Retail", "5–10x", "<4x"], ["E-commerce", "5–8x", "<4x"], ["Manufacturing", "4.5–6x", "<3x"], ["Grocery / Perishable", "14–20x", "<10x"]]},
